{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Professor Gamble buys a lottery ticket, which requires that he pick six different integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abef9fdb0235b2ede2639538b5bd76711e058fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, inclusive. He chooses his numbers so that the sum of the base-ten logarithms of his six numbers is an integer. It so happens that the integers on the winning ticket have the same property— the sum of the base-ten logarithms is an integer. What is the probability that Professor Gamble holds the winner ticket?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c86f45606455a8990e1cf00d27a9be1687f5e9e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf {(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad \\textbf {(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf {(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf {(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf {(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the sum of the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> logarithms of Gamble's numbers is an integer, the product of his numbers must be a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. So each of his numbers has no prime factors other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and thus each of his numbers can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/51569d240781c07fb94a9c83fa10179ffa5782e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m 5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are nonnegative integers. Therefore, all his numbers are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db09a5529602ceb9450528d42dc6304a22085e5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 16, 20, 25, 32, 40\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Define the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/5088ca7351a1dd47a11ecedb0f2678a7e6580357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2^m 5^n) = m - n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" /> whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are nonnegative integers.  Then:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d58adb866ec44c4cfc21e31961dbce0f15e0213c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(25) = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4dba0a2e5c618744f0dac4756e9a1628a9cdbe43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(5) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887724d741033ea9737deab78c3acf44607b88dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = f(10) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2904b5b79c5e75e70e4d9e86818ca2a842515eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = f(20) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847354493404a7005f33b2f71644224a45fa2916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4) = f(40) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c28f929e64e80b765308fae3c838a0b7c8b3040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(8) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c1f3215f56ebcd4d774cdb954f68bea083b770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(16) = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a7e42c3dd314f51137ebc453995663cc24a81e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(32) = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568070f5b996471bfde0f18114b11dce4d50f6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 2^{a_1}5^{b_1}, ..., x_6 = 2^{a_6}5^{b_6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" /> be Gamble's numbers (where all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> are nonnegative integers).  \n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/22351d9a063c01570526c8d0f1304484681456f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1x_2...x_6 = 2^{a_1+a_2+...+a_6}5^{b_1+b_2+...+b_6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"277\" height=\"20\" /> is a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04522fbae1c0597deb8c3e36b10ac400aef37e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2 + ... + a_6 = b_1 + b_2 + ... + b_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"287\" height=\"17\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2c158bb5ef5f5051d73fcd22986b5d8da29f40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1-b_1) + (a_2-b_2) + ... + (a_6-b_6) = f(x_1) + f(x_2) + ... + f(x_6) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"558\" height=\"20\" />.  \n</p><p>The minimum possible sum of any five of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f1c18bb70456045eddcab9dbe67e848c53b428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_1), f(x_2), ..., f(x_6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/58612438c8e3af46f4bf1abdb4b7d4ccc668220c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2) + (-1) + 0 + 0 + 1 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"240\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e15daa4aa18aa1637fac74cb182404b12505ae70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_i)\\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.  This reduces the set of numbers Gamble could have chosen to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3a54ff12bb20096ad329dfc4762f9779a7c599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{1, 2, 4, 5, 10, 20, 25, 40\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />, and Gamble chose all but two of these numbers.\n</p><p>Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe36ee18bba878aa853cc0217ee62775c0f0307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) + f(2) + f(4) + f(5) + f(10) + f(20) + f(25) + f(40) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"500\" height=\"20\" />. So if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae90d71491f591ab5a16d19ee7629e8226ec9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6c5ddfd368673c178f3323ce2994cdbc8fbdab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> are the two numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> that Gamble did not choose, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18a5abdacf87bcb955f55229077879f8c51d120f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(s_1) + f(s_2) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />.  So Gamble chose all the numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> except one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a9174f2fdbb3277ac0d26d548036c4984c27ce67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2, 20\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"20\" /> and one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc2cd1a2c70842352e7211c6a73c954c0d9e98e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{4, 40\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible sets of numbers Gamble could have chosen, so his probability of winning is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8c0715bbd6a8b0e49d6200b213e8eb6d823c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4TCwjl8c7kA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4TCwjl8c7kA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/9vP9Efu18Jk\">https://youtu.be/9vP9Efu18Jk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12\">2000 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163226\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 323/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8464/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.964      1 -total\n 57.29%    8.000      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 41.19%    5.752      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6141:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163226 and revision id 283578. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}